    "abstract": "MAE masks random patches of the input image (75%) and reconstructs the missing pixels. An asymmetric encoder-decoder design applies the ViT encoder only to visible patches and uses a lightweight decoder with mask tokens. High masking ratios make the pretext task non-trivial and speed up training by 3x or more. A vanilla ViT-Huge reaches 87.8% ImageNet-1K accuracy after fine-tuning using only ImageNet-1K data.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "Masking a high proportion of patches (75%) yields a nontrivial and meaningful self-supervisory task.",
      "An asymmetric design with the encoder on visible patches only and a lightweight decoder accelerates training by 3x or more.",
      "ViT-Huge pretrained with MAE reaches 87.8% top-1 on ImageNet-1K (448 px fine-tuning) using only ImageNet-1K data.",
      "Reconstructing per-patch normalized pixels improves representation quality.",
      "MAE transfers well to detection, segmentation, and classification, outperforming supervised pretraining."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
